  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. aluminum exports were $13.67B in 2025 (−5.2%) and are up 25% in January–August 2026; scrap (7602, $4.46B) is the largest product, sold mostly to Thailand, India, Malaysia, Hong Kong and South Korea.",
    "Scrap pays 0% in Thailand, Malaysia, Korea and Hong Kong and 2.5–5% in India, but 35% in China; buyers' purity, inspection and permit rules (China's recycled-aluminum standard, Malaysia's SIRIM certificate, India's pre-shipment inspection, Thailand's container checks) decide whether a load clears.",
    "Canada ($3.03B) has charged a 50% surtax on most U.S. aluminum since September 8, 2026, with no CUSMA exemption; scrap, cans and gas cylinders are exempt, and aluminum imported before July 1, 2027 for Canadian manufacturing or food and beverage packaging can have it remitted.",
    "Mexico ($3.83B) still takes qualifying aluminum free under USMCA, but U.S. hollow profiles pay a US$1.72/kg anti-dumping duty since September 2026, and Mexico's general rates on many aluminum lines rose to 25–35% in 2026."
